{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And he refused to be comforted.</b> Rashi explained that it was specifically regarding the dead that a decree was decreed that he be forgotten from the heart, and not regarding the living — that he [Jacob] supposed him dead. And the reason for this is that the essence of comfort is when the living takes to heart that this dead one has merited the abundance of good hidden away for the righteous, and that he has been transported from the dark world to the eternal light, as it is written (Psalms 84:11): ״כִּי טוֹב יוֹם בַּחֲצֵרֶיךָ מֵאָלֶף״ etc. And Jacob saw in the holy spirit that Joseph was not in Gan Eden; therefore ״וַיְמָאֵן לְהִתְנַחֵם״. And he gave a reason for the matter: ״כִּי אֵרֵד אֶל בְּנִי אָבֵל שְׁאֹלָה״. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said (see Tanḥuma Vayigash 9) that he said this because he had been assured that he would not see the face of Gehinnom as long as one of his sons did not die. And this is difficult: he should have said ״כִּי אֵרֵד אָבֵל שְׁאֹלָה״ — for since he said ״אֶל בְּנִי״, it implies that his son too is in the netherworld of Gehinnom, and from where did Jacob learn to say such a thing? Rather, it is certain that because he saw that his son was not in Gan Eden, he reasoned that he must certainly be in Gehinnom, and I too will go down to him there. Therefore ״וַיְמָאֵן לְהִתְנַחֵם״ — even regarding his son alone. And some press the question: if so, why did Jacob not sense through this that he [Joseph] was alive? And it appears that this is not difficult at all, even according to its plain sense, for Jacob suspended the matter on the fear of seeing the face of Gehinnom, which was before his eyes constantly, because a sign had been handed down to him: that as long as one of his sons did not die in his lifetime, he would not see the face of Gehinnom. This is what he said: ״כִּי אֵרֵד אֶל בְּנִי אָבֵל שְׁאֹלָה״. Nevertheless, the verse ״נִשְׁכַּחְתִּי כְּמֵת מִלֵּב״ (Psalms 31:13) implies actually dead. Therefore Rashi explained the reason that is according to the truth, and not the reason that is according to Jacob's supposition."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:32:27.523934502Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}